            "content": "# Docker Deployment Guide\n\nThis guide explains how to build and deploy the use-ai-server-app using Docker.\n\n## Prerequisites\n\n- Docker 20.10 or later\n- Docker Compose (optional, for easier deployment)\n- At least one AI provider API key (Anthropic or OpenAI)\n\n## Quick Start with Docker Compose\n\n1. **Copy environment variables:**\n   ```bash\n   cd apps/use-ai-server-app\n   cp .env.example .env\n   ```\n\n2. **Edit `.env` and add your API keys:**\n   ```bash\n   # Required: At least one API key\n   ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=your_key_here\n   ```\n\n3. **Start the server:**\n   ```bash\n   docker-compose up -d\n   ```\n\n4. **Check logs:**\n   ```bash\n   docker-compose logs -f\n   ```\n\n5. **Stop the server:**\n   ```bash\n   docker-compose down\n   ```\n\n## Building the Docker Image Manually\n\nThe Dockerfile must be run from the **monorepo root** because it needs access to workspace dependencies:\n\n```bash\n# From the monorepo root (/home/z/Desktop/work/use-ai)\ndocker build -f apps/use-ai-server-app/Dockerfile -t use-ai-server:latest .\n```\n\n### Build Arguments\n\nThe image uses Bun 1.3.2 as specified in the monorepo's `package.json`.\n\n## Running the Container Manually\n\n```bash\ndocker run -d \\\n  --name use-ai-server \\\n  -p 8081:8081 \\\n  -e ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=your_key_here \\\n  -e LOG_FORMAT=json \\\n  use-ai-server:latest\n```\n\n### Environment Variables\n\n**Required (at least one):**\n- `ANTHROPIC_API_KEY` - Anthropic API key for Claude\n- `OPENAI_API_KEY` - OpenAI API key for GPT\n\n**Optional:**\n- `ANTHROPIC_MODEL` - Claude model (default: `claude-sonnet-4-20250514`)\n- `OPENAI_MODEL` - OpenAI model (default: `gpt-4-turbo`)\n- `PORT` - Server port (default: `8081`)\n- `LOG_FORMAT` - Log format: `pretty` or `json` (default: `json`)\n- `RATE_LIMIT_MAX_REQUESTS` - Max requests per window (0 = unlimited, default: `0`)\n- `RATE_LIMIT_WINDOW_MS` - Rate limit window in ms (default: `60000`)\n- `LANGFUSE_PUBLIC_KEY` - Langfuse public key for observability\n- `LANGFUSE_SECRET_KEY` - Langfuse secret key for observability\n- `LANGFUSE_BASE_URL` - Langfuse base URL (default: `https://cloud.langfuse.com`)\n- `DIFY_API_URL` - Dify API URL for workflow integration\n- `DIFY_<WORKFLOW>_KEY` - Dify workflow keys (e.g., `DIFY_GREETING_WORKFLOW_KEY`)\n- `MCP_ENDPOINT_<NAME>_URL` - MCP server URL\n- `MCP_ENDPOINT_<NAME>_NAMESPACE` - MCP server namespace\n- `MCP_ENDPOINT_<NAME>_TIMEOUT` - MCP server timeout in ms\n\n## Multi-Architecture Builds\n\nTo build for multiple architectures (e.g., for deployment on ARM64 servers):\n\n```bash\ndocker buildx build \\\n  --platform linux/amd64,linux/arm64 \\\n  -f apps/use-ai-server-app/Dockerfile \\\n  -t use-ai-server:latest \\\n  --push \\\n  .\n```\n\n## Publishing to a Registry\n\n### Docker Hub\n\n```bash\n# Tag the image\ndocker tag use-ai-server:latest your-username/use-ai-server:latest\ndocker tag use-ai-server:latest your-username/use-ai-server:0.1.1\n\n# Push to Docker Hub\ndocker push your-username/use-ai-server:latest\ndocker push your-username/use-ai-server:0.1.1\n```\n\n### GitHub Container Registry (ghcr.io)\n\n```bash\n# Login to GitHub Container Registry\necho $GITHUB_TOKEN | docker login ghcr.io -u USERNAME --password-stdin\n\n# Tag the image\ndocker tag use-ai-server:latest ghcr.io/your-org/use-ai-server:latest\ndocker tag use-ai-server:latest ghcr.io/your-org/use-ai-server:0.1.1\n\n# Push to GitHub Container Registry\ndocker push ghcr.io/your-org/use-ai-server:latest\ndocker push ghcr.io/your-org/use-ai-server:0.1.1\n```\n\n### Private Registry\n\n```bash\n# Tag the image\ndocker tag use-ai-server:latest registry.example.com/use-ai-server:latest\n\n# Push to private registry\ndocker push registry.example.com/use-ai-server:latest\n```\n\n## Kubernetes Deployment\n\nExample Kubernetes deployment:\n\n```yaml\napiVersion: apps/v1\nkind: Deployment\nmetadata:\n  name: use-ai-server\nspec:\n  replicas: 3\n  selector:\n    matchLabels:\n      app: use-ai-server\n  template:\n    metadata:\n      labels:\n        app: use-ai-server\n    spec:\n      containers:\n      - name: use-ai-server\n        image: use-ai-server:latest\n        ports:\n        - containerPort: 8081\n        env:\n        - name: ANTHROPIC_API_KEY\n          valueFrom:\n            secretKeyRef:\n              name: use-ai-secrets\n              key: anthropic-api-key\n        - name: LOG_FORMAT\n          value: \"json\"\n        resources:\n          requests:\n            memory: \"256Mi\"\n            cpu: \"100m\"\n          limits:\n            memory: \"512Mi\"\n            cpu: \"500m\"\n        livenessProbe:\n          httpGet:\n            path: /health\n            port: 8081\n          initialDelaySeconds: 10\n          periodSeconds: 30\n        readinessProbe:\n          httpGet:\n            path: /health\n            port: 8081\n          initialDelaySeconds: 5\n          periodSeconds: 10\n---\napiVersion: v1\nkind: Service\nmetadata:\n  name: use-ai-server\nspec:\n  selector:\n    app: use-ai-server\n  ports:\n  - port: 8081\n    targetPort: 8081\n  type: LoadBalancer\n```\n\nCreate the secret:\n```bash\nkubectl create secret generic use-ai-secrets \\\n  --from-literal=anthropic-api-key=your_key_here\n```\n\n## Health Check\n\nThe container includes a health check endpoint. You can verify the server is running:\n\n```bash\ncurl http://localhost:8081/health\n```\n\n## Troubleshooting\n\n### View logs\n```bash\ndocker logs -f use-ai-server\n```\n\n### Check if container is running\n```bash\ndocker ps | grep use-ai-server\n```\n\n### Inspect container\n```bash\ndocker inspect use-ai-server\n```\n\n### Access container shell\n```bash\ndocker exec -it use-ai-server /bin/sh\n```\n\n### Check health status\n```bash\ndocker inspect --format='{{json .State.Health}}' use-ai-server\n```\n\n## Security Considerations\n\n- The container runs as a non-root user (`bunuser`, UID 1001) for security\n- API keys should be passed via environment variables or secrets management systems\n- Use `.env` files only for local development (never commit them to git)\n- In production, use Kubernetes secrets, AWS Secrets Manager, or similar\n- Enable rate limiting in production environments\n- Use HTTPS/WSS for WebSocket connections in production\n\n## Performance Optimization\n\n- The multi-stage build minimizes the final image size\n- Only production dependencies are included\n- Built artifacts are copied, not source files\n- Consider using a CDN or load balancer for multiple instances\n- For horizontal scaling, use sticky sessions or Redis adapter for Socket.IO\n\n## Image Size\n\nThe production image is optimized for size:\n- Uses `oven/bun:1.3.2-slim` base image\n- Multi-stage build excludes dev dependencies and source files\n- Typical size: ~200-300MB (depending on dependencies)\n",
