            "content": "# UseAI Server App\n\nStandalone server application for running the UseAI Socket.IO server. This server coordinates between client applications and AI agents (Claude, GPT, etc.) and supports workflow integrations.\n\n## Features\n\n- Multiple AI provider support (Anthropic Claude, OpenAI GPT)\n- Pluggable workflow integration (Dify, etc.)\n- MCP (Model Context Protocol) endpoint support\n- Rate limiting and security features\n- Langfuse observability integration\n- Production-ready Docker container\n\n## Quick Start\n\n### Local Development\n\n```bash\n# Install dependencies (from monorepo root)\nbun install\n\n# Set required environment variables\nexport ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=your_key_here\n\n# Run the server\nbun run dev\n```\n\nThe server will start on http://localhost:8081\n\n### Docker Deployment\n\nSee [DOCKER.md](./DOCKER.md) for comprehensive Docker deployment documentation.\n\nQuick start with Docker Compose:\n\n```bash\n# Copy and configure environment variables\ncp .env.example .env\n# Edit .env and add your API keys\n\n# Start the server\ndocker-compose up -d\n\n# View logs\ndocker-compose logs -f\n```\n\n### Building Docker Image\n\n```bash\n# Using the build script (recommended)\n./docker-build.sh\n\n# Or manually from monorepo root\ndocker build -f apps/use-ai-server-app/Dockerfile -t use-ai-server:latest .\n```\n\n## Configuration\n\n### Required Environment Variables\n\nAt least one AI provider API key is required:\n- `ANTHROPIC_API_KEY` - Anthropic Claude API key\n- `OPENAI_API_KEY` - OpenAI GPT API key\n\n### Optional Environment Variables\n\n**AI Models:**\n- `ANTHROPIC_MODEL` - Claude model (default: `claude-sonnet-4-20250514`)\n- `OPENAI_MODEL` - OpenAI model (default: `gpt-4-turbo`)\n\n**Server:**\n- `PORT` - Server port (default: `8081`)\n- `LOG_FORMAT` - Log format: `pretty` or `json` (default: `json` in Docker)\n\n**Rate Limiting:**\n- `RATE_LIMIT_MAX_REQUESTS` - Max requests per window, 0 = unlimited (default: `0`)\n- `RATE_LIMIT_WINDOW_MS` - Rate limit window in milliseconds (default: `60000`)\n\n**Observability (Langfuse):**\n- `LANGFUSE_PUBLIC_KEY` - Langfuse public key\n- `LANGFUSE_SECRET_KEY` - Langfuse secret key\n- `LANGFUSE_BASE_URL` - Langfuse URL (default: `https://cloud.langfuse.com`)\n\n**Workflow Integration (Dify):**\n- `DIFY_API_URL` - Dify API base URL\n- `DIFY_<WORKFLOW>_KEY` - Workflow-specific keys (e.g., `DIFY_GREETING_WORKFLOW_KEY`)\n\n**MCP Endpoints:**\n- `MCP_ENDPOINT_<NAME>_URL` - MCP server URL\n- `MCP_ENDPOINT_<NAME>_NAMESPACE` - MCP server namespace\n- `MCP_ENDPOINT_<NAME>_TIMEOUT` - MCP server timeout in ms\n\nSee [.env.example](./.env.example) for a complete example.\n\n## Architecture\n\nThe server acts as a coordinator between:\n1. **Client applications** - React apps using the `@meetsmore/use-ai-client` package\n2. **AI agents** - LLM providers (Claude, GPT) via AI SDK\n3. **Workflow runners** - External workflow engines (Dify, etc.)\n4. **MCP servers** - Model Context Protocol endpoints for extended capabilities\n\nCommunication happens over WebSocket using the AG-UI protocol.\n\n## Scripts\n\n- `bun run dev` - Start development server with hot reload\n- `bun run build` - Build for production\n- `bun run start` - Run production build\n- `./docker-build.sh` - Build and test Docker image\n\n## Documentation\n\n- [DOCKER.md](./DOCKER.md) - Comprehensive Docker deployment guide\n- [.env.example](./.env.example) - Example environment configuration\n- [docker-compose.yml](./docker-compose.yml) - Docker Compose configuration\n- [.github-workflow-example.yml](./.github-workflow-example.yml) - GitHub Actions CI/CD example\n\n## Deployment Platforms\n\nThis server is designed to be deployed on:\n- **Kubernetes** - Full deployment example in DOCKER.md\n- **Docker** - Via docker-compose or standalone containers\n- **Cloud Run / Cloud Functions** - Serverless container platforms\n- **AWS ECS/Fargate** - Container orchestration on AWS\n- **Azure Container Instances** - Container platform on Azure\n\n## Security\n\n- Runs as non-root user (UID 1001)\n- Rate limiting per IP address\n- Environment-based secrets management\n- No sensitive data in logs (when using `LOG_FORMAT=json`)\n\n## Monitoring\n\nThe container includes health checks via Socket.IO connection testing. For production:\n- Enable Langfuse for LLM observability and cost tracking\n- Use structured logging with `LOG_FORMAT=json`\n- Monitor WebSocket connection metrics\n- Set up alerts for rate limiting and errors\n\n## Support\n\nFor issues and questions:\n- Check the [main repository documentation](../../CLAUDE.md)\n- See the [Docker deployment guide](./DOCKER.md)\n- Review environment variable configuration in [.env.example](./.env.example)\n\n## License\n\nPart of the `use-ai` monorepo. See repository root for license information.\n",
